OK      LX2 lab L02: insider-trading fact-pattern classifier. HYPOTHETICAL patterns; rules as coded in this lab.
OK      P1: A director of the issuer learns of an unannounced acquisition agreement and buys shares before any announcement.
OK      P2: A senior officer of the issuer tells a friend about a pending product recall. The officer receives nothing, and the friend trades.
OK      P3: A mid-level employee of the issuer tells a fund manager about a pending merger for a cash payment. The manager trades.
OK      P4: A corporate lawyer gives her brother-in-law advance word of a tender offer, with no payment. He trades.
OK      P5: An officer of the issuer gives a fund manager a tip for a cash payment. The manager has no reason to know of the payment, and trades.
OK      P6: An associate at an accounting firm reads a client's confidential file on a planned acquisition of a target company. He buys the target's shares be
OK      P7: The same associate tells the client in writing that he plans to buy the target's shares, and then buys them.
OK      P8: A stranger overhears two executives discuss a planned acquisition on a train, has no relationship with them, and buys the target's shares.
